      "message": "It is generally frowned upon in Java to pass an object to write into, especially if that\u0027s a member like in line 289. Also :\n• this writes to the mAllApps member but also interacts through the mUidToNetworkPerm member through an argument, which is fairly confusing\n• the call in addUser merges the array into mUidToNetworkPerm without calling isHigherNetworkPermission. This relies on the fact that none of the UIDs were in the member before for correctness.\n\nHere are some suggestions of things to do instead :\n- Call sendUidsNetworkPermission and sendAppIdsTrafficPermission directly in this method (IIUC, it\u0027s fine to always do both and to call once per user)\n- Have a function that returns a List\u003cPackageInfo\u003e, and then separate functions for appId, networkPerms and trafficPerms\n- Return a Pair\n- Pass a List\u003cConsumer\u003cPackageInfo\u003e\u003e to this method, and use method references to make the code inside common",
